## Examining potentially harmful strategies¶

### Quote stuffing¶

Quote-stuffing is a technique whereby a trader floods the market with orders and rapidly cancels them. The ânoiseâ created by the influx of orders can affect other tradersâ latency and create an arbitrage opportunity for the high-frequency trader. If the orders are âstuffedâ within the spread, other traders can perceive a false impression of the market. Quote-stuffing generally occurs in bursts and will last less than 10 seconds on average (Credit Suisse, 2012).


    // - Function to pull back the quote table on a date (dt) for any stock (s)
    // - burstperiod is the length of time we expect the quote-stuffing to occur
    // - pricemovements is the minimum number of movements 
